<title>USA: Viasystems issues $400 mln in 10-year 144A notes.</title>
<headline>Viasystems issues $400 mln in 10-year 144A notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following high-yield 144A debt issue from Viasystems Inc was priced on Monday, according to a syndicate source.</p>
<p>The issue was oversubscribed and upsized by $100 million the source added.</p>
<p>St. Louis, Missouri-based Viasystems manufactures printed circuit boards and backpanels for telecommunications, computer, automotive, military and other industrial uses.</p>
<p>BORROWER VIASYSTEMS INC</p>
<p>AMT $400 MLN	 COUPON 9-3/4 PCT  MATURITY 6/01/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NTS   ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 12/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 9-3/4 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS			   CALLABLE NON CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTE: Three year equity call for 35 percent at par plus coupon</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
</text>
